### 10. vita, kunna, and þekkja
The confusion here is that all of these words translate to *know* in English. However, they are all used seperately. 

*vita* is used for knowing facts and information. It is the broadest category. 

Example 1: Þú veist ekkert um mig. - (You know nothing about me.)\
Example 2: Ég veit alveg hvað ég er að tala um. - (I know exactly what I am talking about.)\
Example 3: Hann viet hvað Hljóðhraðinn er. - (He knows what the speed of sound it.)

*kunna* is used for skills and knowing how to manage things, such as knowing vocabulary words.

Example 1: Hún kann ekki að tefla - (She doesn't know how to play chess).\
Example 2: Ég kann orð yfir dýr, liti og stærð - (I know words for animals, colors, and size).\
Example 3: Ég kann ekki annađ en ađ vera einhleypur. - (I don't know how to be anything other than single.)

*þekkja* is used for being familiar with people, places, and experiences. 
Example 1: Þekkir þú mig? - (Do you know me?)\
Example 2: Hann þekkir Chicago vel. - (He knows Chicago well.)\
Example 3: Hún var blind, en þekkti samt rödd mína. - (She was blind but knew my voice.)

